 "indicator": {
  "definition": {
   "definition": "Bank credit of scheduled commercial banks is the aggregate outstanding loans and advances (in India) of SCBs. In RBI's fortnightly statement it is the sum of food credit and non-food credit — Bank credit = food credit + non-food credit — so food credit is included and non-food credit is bank credit less food credit. RBI compiles it from the fortnightly Form A return furnished by all SCBs under Section 42(2) of the RBI Act, 1934, and publishes it as item 7 'Bank Credit' in the 'Scheduled Commercial Banks — Business in India' statement in the WSS/RBI Bulletin, in rupees crore, provisionally and fortnightly.",
   "source_name": "RBI — A Handbook on RBI's Weekly Statistical Supplement, Section 4: Scheduled Commercial Banks – Business in India",
   "source_url": "https://rbidocs.rbi.org.in/rdocs/Publications/PDFs/HWSSF170614.pdf",
